{#
	"עוד בנושא" — three more articles at the foot of a post. Figma
	`related-posts` (21:195), new in the 2026-09 revision.

	Derived from the query, the same as `next-project` and `pagination`. An
	authored "related" field would be a third list to maintain per post and
	would rot silently: nothing tells an editor that the article they picked
	two years ago has been unpublished.

	`עוד בנושא` is a fixed label on derived navigation, in the same class as
	`הפרויקט הבא` and `מומלץ` — it names the slot, it is not content an editor
	chose.

	The card is category + title and nothing else. No date and no thumbnail:
	the frame draws none, and this row's job is to say what else is here, not
	to re-run the index.

	Params:
	  posts  array of Timber\Post — already filtered and ordered by
	         coweb_related_posts(); empty renders nothing.
#}

{% if posts|length %}
	<nav class="related-posts" aria-labelledby="related-posts-label">
		<div class="container related-posts__inner">
			<p class="related-posts__label" id="related-posts-label">עוד בנושא</p>

			<ul class="related-posts__row" role="list">
				{% for item in posts %}
					<li class="related-card">
						{% set category = item.terms('category')|first %}

						{# The category is a label here, not a link: the card is
						   one target, and a link inside a link is neither. #}
						<p class="related-card__meta">
							{{ category ? category.title : 'בלוג' }}
						</p>

						{# h2: the page's h1 is the article title in the hero. #}
						<h2 class="related-card__title">
							<a class="related-card__link" href="{{ item.link }}"><bdi>{{ item.title }}</bdi></a>
						</h2>
					</li>
				{% endfor %}
			</ul>
		</div>
	</nav>
{% endif %}
